The bug is on line 14: the `break` statement exits the loop after the first matching tracking param is deleted, so any subsequent tracking params (e.g. `fbclid`) remain.

**Fix:** remove the `break` so all tracking params are iterated over and stripped.

The patch has already been applied — the loop now reads:

```ts
for (const param of TRACKING_PARAMS) {
  u.searchParams.delete(param);
}
```

`URLSearchParams.delete()` is a no-op when the key doesn't exist, so the `if` guard is unnecessary. All tracking params present in the URL are now stripped.


